{Sentence 1: "The color gamut of a monitor is defined as the range of colors that it can produce or record."}
{Sentence 2: "The primary colors of a monitor are red, green, and blue, and its color gamut is shown in a triangular area enclosed by these colors on the chromaticity diagram."}
{Sentence 3: "Color gamut is a three-dimensional concept, but it is often represented in two dimensions due to the difficulty of plotting a three-dimensional graph."}
{Sentence 4: "Standardizing a color gamut, such as sRGB, helps ensure consistent color reproduction across different devices."}
{Sentence 5: "Equal color gamut areas do not necessarily guarantee the same color rendering capability; instead, coverage rate should be considered when comparing two color gamuts."}

{Sentence 1: "The color gamut of the new printer is much wider than its predecessor."}
{Sentence 2: "Her eyes had a wide color gamut, able to distinguish between subtle shades of blue and green."}
{Sentence 3: "The artist struggled to capture the full color gamut of the sunset in his painting."}
{Sentence 4: "The camera's color gamut was limited, resulting in less vibrant images compared to high-end models."}
{Sentence 5: "The designer carefully selected colors within the color gamut of the brand's logo to ensure consistent visual identity."}
